# Documentation Integrity Guardrails

## Purpose
Ensure that all executable paths (scripts, commands, services) are documented and mapped. Prevent drift between code and documentation.

## Rules

### 1. When Adding/Modifying Scripts

**Scope**: Any changes to:
- `package.json` scripts section
- Files in `scripts/**/*.{sh,ps1,js,ts}`
- Docker Compose files (`*.yml`, `*docker-compose*.yml`)
- Root-level executable files (`*.sh`, `*.ps1`)

**Required Actions**:

a) **Update Run Paths Catalog**
- File: `docs/50-ops/Run-Paths-Catalog.md`
- Add or update entry with:
  - Unique ID (RP####)
  - Entry name
  - Type (`npm-script`, `shell-script`, `powershell-script`, `docker-service`)
  - Status (`canonical`, `active`, `deprecated`, `shim`, `duplicate`)
  - Description
  - If deprecated: "Replaced By" pointing to canonical command

b) **Update Project Overview**
- File: `docs/00-foundation/Project-Overview.md`
- Section: "Run Workflows (One-Command)"
- Add/update/remove commands as appropriate
- Ensure canonical commands are prominent

c) **Update Module Architecture** (if behavior changes)
- File: `docs/10-architecture/Modules.md`
- Update relevant module sections if script interacts with code modules

d) **Update Docker/Service Docs** (if Docker-related)
- Files: `docs/50-ops/Docker-Services.md`, `docs/50-ops/Service-Health.md`
- Add/update service entries, health checks, ports, configurations

### 2. Regenerate Documentation

After making changes, you MUST run:

```bash
pnpm docs:all
```

This regenerates:
- Dependency maps (`docs/maps/`)
- TypeDoc API docs (`docs/api/`)
- OpenAPI specification (`docs/20-backend/openapi.json`)

### 3. Verify Integrity

Run the documentation integrity checker:

```bash
pnpm check:docs
```

This validates:
- All scripts in `package.json` are documented in Run-Paths-Catalog
- All script files in `scripts/**` are documented
- No deprecated scripts are referenced in docs
- All Docker services are documented

### 4. No Standalone Summary Docs

**NEVER** create standalone "summary" or "complete" docs like:
- `FEATURE_COMPLETE.md`
- `MIGRATION_GUIDE.md` (unless temporary)
- `REFACTOR_SUMMARY.md`
- `SETUP_GUIDE.md`

Instead:
- Edit **canonical docs** directly (Project-Overview.md, Modules.md, Docker-Services.md, etc.)
- If you create a temporary summary for a complex change:
  1. Merge content into canonical docs
  2. Move summary to `docs/_archive/` with a banner pointing to canonical locations
  3. Update the banner to reference specific sections

**Banner Template** for archived docs:
```markdown
> **⚠️ ARCHIVED**: This document has been merged into canonical docs
> 
> See:
> - [Project Overview](../00-foundation/Project-Overview.md#external-services)
> - [Module Architecture](../10-architecture/Modules.md#external-integrations)
> - [Docker Services](../50-ops/Docker-Services.md)
```

### 5. Run Paths Catalog Format

Each entry must include:

| Field | Description | Required |
|-------|-------------|----------|
| ID | Unique identifier (RP####) | ✅ |
| Entry | Command/script name | ✅ |
| Type | npm-script, shell-script, powershell-script, docker-service | ✅ |
| Status | canonical, active, deprecated, shim, duplicate | ✅ |
| Refs | Reference count (grep usage) | Optional |
| Recent | Last commit touching this path | Optional |
| Boot | Is it a bootstrap/entry point? | Optional |
| Overlap | Percentage overlap with other entries | Optional |
| Platform | cross, windows, linux, darwin | Optional |
| Replaced By | Canonical command (if deprecated) | Required for deprecated |

### 6. Enforcement Points

**Pre-commit** (via `pnpm precommit`):
- Runs `pnpm check:docs` to catch missing documentation

**CI Pipeline** (`.github/workflows/docs-and-smoke-min.yml`):
- Runs `pnpm docs:all` to regenerate all docs
- Runs `pnpm check:deps` to validate dependencies
- Runs `pnpm check:docs` to validate documentation integrity

**Cursor AI** (this rule):
- Enforces documentation updates before code changes are "complete"
- Refuses to mark tasks done until docs are updated
- Shows diffs for all documentation changes

## Examples

### Good: Adding a New Script

```typescript
// 1. Add to package.json
"scripts": {
  "deploy:prod": "node scripts/production/deploy.js"
}

// 2. Update docs/50-ops/Run-Paths-Catalog.md
| RP0150 | `deploy:prod` | npm-script | canonical | - | - | - | - | cross | - |

// 3. Update docs/00-foundation/Project-Overview.md
### Production Deployment
```bash
pnpm deploy:prod
```

// 4. Run
pnpm docs:all
pnpm check:docs

// 5. Show diffs and verify
```

### Bad: Creating Standalone Summary

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD: Created DEPLOYMENT_COMPLETE.md -->
# Deployment System Complete

Successfully implemented...

<!-- ✅ GOOD: Edit canonical docs instead -->
Edit docs/00-foundation/Project-Overview.md → Add deployment section
Edit docs/50-ops/Run-Paths-Catalog.md → Add deployment scripts
```

### Good: Deprecating a Script

```typescript
// 1. Mark as deprecated in Run-Paths-Catalog.md
| RP0042 | `start-local.ps1` | powershell-script | deprecated | - | - | - | - | windows | `scripts/win/start-local.ps1` |

// 2. Update script to redirect
Write-Host "⚠️ DEPRECATED: Use scripts/win/start-local.ps1 instead"
& scripts/win/start-local.ps1 @args

// 3. Update Project-Overview.md to remove from main workflows
// 4. Run integrity check
pnpm check:docs
```

## Consequences of Non-Compliance

- **CI Failure**: Pipeline fails if `check:docs` detects undocumented scripts
- **Review Rejection**: PRs without documentation updates will be rejected
- **Drift Detection**: Automated sweeps will flag undocumented commands

